{{page-title "Display"}}

{{!-- Display: block --}}
<div class="layout__section">
  <div class="layout__header">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <code>display: block</code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        How does this work?
      </div>

      <div class="section__description">
        <p>
          <code>display: block</code> is the default value for most elements. It will make the element behave like a
          block-level element. This means that the element will take up the full width of the parent element and will
          start on a new line.
        </p>

        <p>
          Notice how in the example below, there are two boxes that could be side by side, but because they are block
          elements, they are stacked on top of each other.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="section__body">
        <div class="demo-container" style="background: lightgray;">
          <div class="demo-item" style="width: 500px;">
            <div class="demo-item demo-item--base" style="width: 40%;">
              <div class="demo-item demo-item--block" style="background: indianred;">
                Box A
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
          <div class="demo-item" style="width: 500px;">
            <div class="demo-item demo-item--base" style="width: 40%;">
              <div class="demo-item demo-item--block" style="background: mediumaquamarine;">
                Box B
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{{!-- end Display: block --}}

{{!-- Display: inline --}}
<div class="layout__section">
  <div class="layout__header">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <code>display: inline</code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        How does this work?
      </div>

      <div class="section__description">
        <p>
          <code>display: inline</code> is the default value for some elements. It will make the element behave like an
          inline element. This means that the element will only take up as much width as necessary and will not start on
          a new line.
        </p>

        <p>
          Notice how in the example below, elements are not affected by <code>width</code> and are displayed inline.
        </p>

        <p>
          There are other properties that do not affect <code>display: inline</code> elements, such as
          <code>margin</code> and <code>width</code>. For margin, inline elements needs to use
          <code>margin-inline</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="section__body">
        <div class="demo-container" style="background: lightgray;">
          <div class="demo-item demo-item--inline" style="width: 500px; background: indianred;">
            Box A
          </div>

          <div class="demo-item demo-item--inline" style="width: 500px; background: mediumaquamarine;">
            Box B
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{{!-- end Display: inline --}}

{{!-- Display: inline-block --}}
<div class="layout__section">
  <div class="layout__header">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <code>display: inline-block</code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        How does this work?
      </div>

      <div class="section__description">
        <p>
          <code>display: inline-block</code> is a combination of <code>display: inline</code> and <code>display:
          block</code>.
          It will make the element behave like an inline element, but you can also set the width and height of the
          element.
        </p>

        <p>
          Notice how in the example below, both boxes are displayed inline, but you can set the width and height of each
          element.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="section__body">
        <div class="demo-container" style="background: lightgray;">
          <div class="demo-item demo-item--inline-block" style="width: 500px; background: indianred;">
            Box A
          </div>

          <div class="demo-item demo-item--inline-block" style="width: 500px; background: mediumaquamarine;">
            Box B
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{{!-- end Display: inline-block --}}

{{!-- Display: flex --}}
<div class="layout__section layout__section--flex-demo">
  <div class="layout__header">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <code>display: flex</code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        How does this work?
      </div>

      <div class="section__description">
        <p>
          <code>display: flex</code> is a layout model that allows elements to align and distribute space within a
          container. It is a powerful layout model that can be used to create complex layouts.
        </p>

        <p>
          Notice how in the example below, both boxes are displayed inside a flex layout. You can set the width and
          height of each element, and you can also align and distribute space within the container.
        </p>

        <p>
          Check the controls below to change different flex-box properties and see how children element behave
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="section__body">
        <div
          class="demo-container demo-container--flex"
          style="
            height: 500px;
            background: lightgray;
            align-items: {{this.alignItems}};
            flex-direction: {{this.flexDirection}};
            justify-content: {{this.justifyContent}};
            "
        >
          <div class="demo-item demo-item--block" style="height: 100px; width: 100px; background: indianred;">
            Box A
          </div>

          <div class="demo-item demo-item--block" style="height: 100px; width: 100px; background: mediumaquamarine;">
            Box B
          </div>

          <div class="demo-item demo-item--block" style="height: 100px; width: 100px; background: greenyellow;">
            Box C
          </div>

          <div class="demo-item demo-item--block" style="height: 100px; width: 100px; background: deeppink;">
            Box D
          </div>

          <div class="demo-item demo-item--block" style="height: 100px; width: 100px; background: skyblue;">
            Box E
          </div>

          <div class="demo-item demo-item--block" style="height: 100px; width: 100px; background: teal;">
            Box F
          </div>

          <div class="demo-item demo-item--block" style="height: 100px; width: 100px; background: royalblue;">
            Box G
          </div>

          <div class="demo-item demo-item--block" style="height: 100px; width: 100px; background: mediumpurple;">
            Box H
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section__controls">
          <div class="section__controls__title">
            Controls
          </div>

          <div class="section__controls__input section__controls__input--inline">
            <select name="flex-direction" {{on 'input' this.updateFlexDirection}}>
              <option>flex-direction</option>
              <option value="row">flex-direction: row</option>
              <option value="row-reverse">flex-direction: row-reverse</option>
              <option value="column">flex-direction: column</option>
              <option value="column-reverse">flex-direction: column-reverse</option>
            </select>
          </div>

          <div class="section__controls__input section__controls__input--inline">
            <select name="justify-content" {{on 'input' this.updateJustifyContent}}>
              <option>justify-content</option>
              <option value="flex-start">justify-content: flex-start</option>
              <option value="flex-end">justify-content: flex-end</option>
              <option value="center">justify-content: center</option>
              <option value="baseline">justify-content: baseline</option>
              <option value="stretch">justify-content: stretch</option>
              <option value="space-between">justify-content: space-between</option>
              <option value="space-around">justify-content: space-around</option>
              <option value="space-evenly">justify-content: space-evenly</option>
            </select>
          </div>

          <div class="section__controls__input section__controls__input--inline">
            <select name="align-items" {{on 'input' this.updateAlignItems}}>
              <option>align-items</option>
              <option value="flex-start">align-items: flex-start</option>
              <option value="flex-end">align-items: flex-end</option>
              <option value="center">align-items: center</option>
              <option value="baseline">align-items: baseline</option>
              <option value="stretch">align-items: stretch</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{{!-- end Display: flex --}}

{{!-- flex items --}}
<div class="layout__section layout__section--flex-demo">
  <div class="layout__header">
    <div class="layout__container">
      flex-item properties
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        Flex items are also affected by flex properties
      </div>

      <div class="section__description">
        <p>
          There are several CSS properties that can be applied to flex items. These properties can be used to control
          the size, order, and alignment of flex items.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="section__body">
        <div
          class="demo-container demo-container--flex"
          style="height: 500px; background: lightgray;"
        >
          <div
            class="demo-item demo-item--block demo-item--no-width"
            style="
              min-height: 100px;
              min-width: 100px;
              background: darkorange;
              flex-grow: {{this.flexItemFlexGrow}};
              align-self: {{this.flexItemAlignSelf}};
            ">
            Box A
          </div>

          <div
            class="demo-item demo-item--block demo-item--no-width"
            style="
              min-height: 100px;
              min-width: 100px;
              background: mediumaquamarine;
              flex-grow: {{this.flexItemFlexGrow}};
              align-self: {{this.flexItemAlignSelf}};
              ">
            Box B
          </div>

          <div
            class="demo-item demo-item--block demo-item--no-width"
            style="
              min-height: 100px;
              min-width: 100px;
              background: darkcyan;
              flex-grow: {{this.flexItemFlexGrow}};
              align-self: {{this.flexItemAlignSelf}};
              ">
            Box C
          </div>

          <div
            class="demo-item demo-item--block demo-item--no-width"
            style="
              min-height: 100px;
              min-width: 100px;
              background: mediumpurple;
              flex-grow: {{this.flexItemFlexGrow}};
              align-self: {{this.flexItemAlignSelf}};
              ">
            Box D
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section__controls">
          <div class="section__controls__title">
            Controls on Children
          </div>

          <div class="section__controls__input section__controls__input--inline">
            <select name="flex-item-grow" {{on 'input' this.updateFlexItemFlexGrow}}>
              <option>flex-grow</option>
              <option value="0">flex-grow: 0</option>
              <option value="1">flex-grow: 1</option>
            </select>
          </div>

          <div class="section__controls__input section__controls__input--inline">
            <select name="align-self" {{on 'input' this.updateFlexItemAlignSelf}}>
              <option>align-self</option>
              <option value="flex-start">align-self: flex-start</option>
              <option value="flex-end">align-self: flex-end</option>
              <option value="center">align-self: center</option>
              <option value="baseline">align-self: baseline</option>
              <option value="stretch">align-self: stretch</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{{!-- end flex items --}}